        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> How would that work if I want to have it set to a custom mapping?\r\n> \r\n> Example:\r\n> \r\n> ```lua\r\n>     pick.registry.lsp_references = function()\r\n>       extra.pickers.lsp({ scope = 'references' })\r\n>     end\r\n>     vim.keymap.set('n', ',r', pick.registry.lsp_references)\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nThere is no need to create a custom registry entry specifically for that mapping. It is enough to do something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set('n', ',r', '<Cmd>Pick lsp scope=\"references\"<CR>')\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat's what [I use](https://github.com/echasnovski/nvim/blob/0a8c9664f0c3d42f0ac912d530d9dd46ee6ae95e/src/mappings-leader.lua#L72).",
